BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Journey to Space" Ribbon Cutting
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261114T000000
DTSTAMP:20261113T190134Z
UID:e1ad88b2e4e6141d76def5b6fe3377@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Journey to Space Ribbon Cutting and Exhibit Opening Saturday\,
  November 14\, 2026 11:00am – 11:30am The EcoTarium is excited to announ
 ce our newest traveling exhibit\, Journey to Space . Come to the official 
 opening and ribbon cutting on Saturday\, November 14\, 2026 at 11:00 am an
 d be among the first to experience this exciting new interactive exhibit! 
 Visitors will discover and explore the exciting environment of outer space
  in Journey to Space ! This highly interactive experience utilizes hands-o
 n elements that allow visitors to work with drop towers\, water rockets\, 
 and robotic arms\, while educating on topics like artificial gravity\, orb
 ital physics\, Newton’s third law of motion\, and more! There’s much t
 o discover as visitors learn more about these immersive topics which explo
 re a variety of challenges and accomplishments\, and show how far we have 
 come in the last fifty years of exploring space. Can’t make our event? D
 on’t worry! We always have something new happening outside\, inside\, an
 d onstage. The Journey to Space exhibit will be sticking around until Apri
 l 2027! Come check it out or experience one of our daily planetarium progr
 ams*\, take a ride on the seasonal Worcester Railers Explorer Express Trai
 n*\, and get up close to our resident otters*! * Requires a separate ticke
 t that is not included with admission. Learn More about the exhibit! This 
 exhibit is included with admission to the EcoTarium on weekdays. On weeken
 ds\, a ticket is required for entry into the Stoddard Exhibition Hall for 
 this exhibit. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://
 www.discovercentralma.org/event/journey-to-space-ribbon-cutting/31017/\n\n
 Events Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Loc
 al fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discov
 ercentralma.org/event/journey-to-space-ribbon-cutting/31017/
LOCATION:EcoTarium\, 222 Harrington Way\, Worcester\, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/journey-to-space-ribbon-cuttin
 g/31017/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Making Paleolithic Cave Art: Teen Saturdays Workshop
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261212T000000
DTSTAMP:20261113T190134Z
UID:9287acf8fff8ade7a1f1040c186134@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Journey 30\,000 years into the past to discover how ancient hu
 mans used art to express themselves\, connect with their environment\, and
  develop techniques and materials to decorate cave walls in Europe. Guided
  by Marlena Billings\, a PhD student in the Department of Anthropology\, t
 eens will explore examples of cave art and learn how archaeologists use ex
 perimental archaeology and microscopes to study how people manufactured ar
 t. Through hands-on activities\, participants will experiment with differe
 nt tools\, surfaces\, and light to see how ancient artists brought animals
  and scenes to life in dark cave spaces. Teen Saturdays Workshops are offe
 red bilingually in Spanish and English. They are designed to build communi
 ty and improve the museum experience for multicultural teens. Snacks provi
 ded! $10 fee includes free admission to all HMSC museums immediately follo
 wing the workshop. Teens will receive a free admission pass (worth $15) fo
 r a return visit if they attend one of the three sessions. October 17: Kna
 pping the First Tools: Teen Saturdays Workshop November 14: Making Paleoli
 thic Cave Art December 12: Animal Stories from the Past Presented by the P
 eabody Museum of Archaeology & Ethnology and the Harvard Museums of Scienc
 e & Culture. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: htt
 ps://www.meetboston.com/event/making-paleolithic-cave-art%3a-teen-saturday
