BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:November Reception: Small Works 2026 and Drinks on Me
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261114T000000
DTSTAMP:20261113T190134Z
UID:ad8639b06882a60ab10ab98b44b842@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our November Reception\, celebrating two new exhib
 itions at ArtsWorcester: The annual favorite Small Works\, and Amanda (And
 i) Pickler's solo exhibition Drinks on Me. Saturday\, November 14\, 2 - 5 
 PM ArtsWorcester\, 44 Portland St\, Worcester MA // Small Works 2026: A Me
 mbers' Exhibition This showcase of miniature works from ArtsWorcester arti
 st members\, ranging in theme and medium. All works are 10"x10" or under. 
 Do your holiday shopping (small works make unique\, wonderful gifts!) or c
 ome simply to explore these small treasures. // Amanda (Andi) Pickler: Dri
 nks on Me In Drinks on Me\, interdisciplinary artist Amanda (Andi) Pickler
  explores the spectrum of intimacy that exists within the domesticity of i
 nterpersonal relationships\, and the public and private spaces of queer ni
 ghtlife. Pickler's saturated\, jewel-toned paintings and detailed prints i
 nclude scenes from her trips to lesbian and queer bars around the country.
  These images and the spaces they depict offer connection\, joy\, and resp
 ite to a community experiencing significant challenges and threats. This e
 vent is free and open to all. Following the reception and beginning at 5:0
 0 PM\, an afterparty will be held at Femme Bar Worcester. Connect with the
  artist of Drinks on Me and see the Worcester bar that inspired some of An
 di's artworks. Small Works 2026 and Drinks on Me will be on view at ArtsWo
 rcester through December 13 during gallery hours: Wednesdays through Sunda
 ys\, each day from 12 PM to 5 PM (always free and open to all). On Decembe
 r 10\, ArtsWorcester will be open until 7PM for late night hours. Concurre
 ntly on view through the duration of the exhibition run will be the Assets
  for Artists 2026 Showcase\, on view in the third floor Davis Art Gallery.
  Parking is available at the Worcester Public Library (McGrath) Lot\, Fede
 ral Plaza Garage\, Worcester Common Garage\, and Pearl-Elm Garage. Metered
  street parking is also available. On weekends\, and on weekdays after 5:0
 0 PM\, visitors may park in the Printers Building parking lot free of char
 ge. Please do not park in the lot across the street from the Printers Buil
 ding\; you will be immediately towed. // Photos: Andi Pickler\, They Don't
  Get To Tell Us Whether Or Not This Is Real\, oil on canvas\, 48" x 26"\, 
 2026 Andi Pickler\, Our Hands At Ginger's\, oil on panel\, 14" x 18"\, 202
 5 Sarah Beard\, It Started to Clear Part Way Up\, 9" x 9"\, acrylic and co
 llage\, 2025 Marjorie Hart\, Hand woven purse with chain handle\, bamboo a
 nd cotton\, 8" x 8" x 0.5"\, 2024 Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts 
 Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/november-reception%3a-
 small-works-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31070/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mile
 s of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts
 -events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/november
 -reception%3a-small-works-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31070/
LOCATION:ArtsWorcester\, 44 Portland St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/november-reception%3a-small-wo
 rks-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31070/
