BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Festivals of Drunkenness in the Temple of Mut
DTSTART:20261118T000000
DTEND:20261118T000000
DTSTAMP:20261113T190134Z
UID:f75adc298dc1b41dfc175af0b07a86@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The Temple of Mut is an ancient Egyptian sanctuary dedicated t
 o the mother goddess Mut. From the early New Kingdom (c. 15th century BCE)
  through the Roman era\, this temple was the setting for several festivals
  of drunkenness. The archaeological remains of a columned hall at Mut’s 
 temple indicate that these celebrations took place during the reign of Que
 en Hatshepsut (c. 1479–1459 BCE). These included the annual Drunkenness 
 Festival and the major Theban ritual known as the Beautiful Feast of the V
 alley. In this lecture\, Betsy Bryan examines how these festivals were cel
 ebrated at Mut and at other sites in ancient Egypt\, highlighting their pa
 rticipants\, rituals\, and religious purposes. Geological Lecture Hall\, 2
 4 Oxford Street\, Cambridge\, MA. Free admission. Free event parking is av
 ailable with registration. Register by November 17 to receive parking regi
 stration instructions.. Presented by the Harvard Museum of the Ancient Nea
 r East and the Harvard Museums of Science and Culture. Speaker: Betsy M. B
 ryan\, Alexander Badawy Professor Emerita of Egyptian Art and Archaeology
 \, Johns Hopkins University LEARN MORE Sources: Meet Boston Event page: ht
 tps://www.meetboston.com/event/the-festivals-of-drunkenness-in-the-temple-
 of-mut/94148/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 0153
 2\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: h
 ttps://www.meetboston.com/event/the-festivals-of-drunkenness-in-the-temple
 -of-mut/94148/
LOCATION:Harvard Museums of Science & Culture\, Geological Lecture Hall 24
  Oxford Street\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-festivals-of-drunkenness-in-the-t
 emple-of-mut/94148/
END:VEVENT
